  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; before starting. Coordinate with 058 on `tests/e2e/pages/`.</protocol>
  </execution>

  <status-note date="2026-09-28">
    COMPLETED WITH ESCALATION. Full record: notes/074-e2e.md.

    OUTCOME: all three Office e2e specs are classified NOT-RUNS-IN-CI, marked in-file, and
    listed in notes/parity-checklist.md section 10. Nothing was wired into the workflow,
    deliberately. 109 tests (32 word + 48 outlook save + 29 outlook share) currently run
    NOWHERE -- no workflow executes tests/e2e at all.

    DETERMINED EMPIRICALLY, as the constraint required, and the easy wrong answer was
    available: .env.example asks for CLIENT_SECRET, TEST_USER_PASSWORD and TENANT_ID, which
    LOOKS like proof a live tenant is needed. The code says otherwise -- the specs default
    to localhost:3000, there are 24 route interceptions (the BFF is mocked),
    mockWordEnvironment() injects window.Office/window.Word, and the build's four required
    env values are PLAIN TEXT in deploy-office-addins.yml:66-69 (public client IDs and a
    URL, not secrets). So I ran them: npm install at root (Playwright was declared there and
    NOT installed), playwright install chromium, built the add-in with those four values,
    served dist/ on 127.0.0.1:3000 (HTTP 200), ran the word spec on chromium.

    RESULT: every test failed with page.waitForFunction timeout. A timeout does not say why,
    so I probed the page: it BOOTS and stalls at "Loading..." with NO page errors --
    "Stage 1: Waiting for Office.js" -> "Office.js is loaded outside of Office client" ->
    "Office.js ready: {host: null, platform: null, addin: null}" -> "Stage 2: Initializing
    auth service" and stops.

    TWO BLOCKERS, both in the HARNESS rather than the specs' intent: (1) the spec DOES apply
    its mock in beforeEach before navigating, but NOTHING intercepts the real office.js CDN
    script -- grep for appsforoffice/office.js across spec and page object returns ZERO -- so
    the real script supersedes the mock and host detection reports host:null; (2) the
    bootstrap then awaits MSAL, which cannot settle headless. A third, smaller defect
    recorded for whoever fixes those: the readiness probe waits for
    [data-fui-focus-visible], which Fluent v9 sets on KEYBOARD FOCUS, not on mount, so even
    a rendered pane might never satisfy it.

    WHICH HALF OF THE TRIGGER FIRED, precisely: NOT the infrastructure half -- no test tenant
    and no hosted add-in are required. The PARALLEL-HARNESS half. Making these run needs
    office.js route-blocking, a completed Office mock, a readiness-probe fix, a CI job, and
    -- the reason this is not a tidy-up -- a TEST SEAM IN THE ADD-IN'S AUTH SERVICE so
    bootstrap can proceed without MSAL. That is a production change to an auth path, CLAUDE.md
    section 6 territory in its own right, and must not be smuggled in under a CI-wiring task.
    Costed in the note (~2.5 days). OWNER DECISION NEEDED: fund it as its own task, or accept
    these as live-host-manual and let task 042's UAT be where they earn their keep.

    CRITERIA DISPOSITION, stated rather than silently skipped: 1 done; 2 VACUOUS (no spec
    qualifies, nothing wired); 3 N/A and cannot be otherwise -- there is no running spec to
    break, so the both-directions proof is impossible, recorded not dropped; 4 done (three
    in-file markers + parity-checklist section 10); 5 classified, not green; 6 actionlint
    unchanged because the workflow was NOT modified. The POML lists the workflow as an edit
    target; adding a job that runs zero specs, or one that runs failing specs, would be worse
    than adding nothing. Deviation recorded.

    058 COORDINATION: the POML asks to coordinate on tests/e2e/pages/addins/
    OutlookTaskPanePage.ts:305-331. 058 is BLOCKED (delete-vs-modify contention with
    unified-access-control-r2), so there is nothing to coordinate with yet. Whoever unblocks
    058 must keep these markers alive through the page-object deletion.

    DRIVE-BY: package.json's lint:fix still read `eslint src` -- the same nonexistent-directory
    defect task 072 fixed in `lint`, left behind because 072's criteria named only one script.
    Fixed. Leaving a known-identical bug on the adjacent line is the inconsistency this wave
    exists to remove.
  
    OWNER DECISION 2026-09-28, escalation CLOSED: "we don't need 109 tests every CI for this
    - we'll manual test when deployed". The ~2.5-day harness work is DECLINED, including the
    auth test seam -- which also removes that production auth-path risk. The specs stay
    classified and marked; they are live-verification items for task 042's UAT, where the
    in-file markers are now the permanent answer rather than a placeholder. Do not wire them
    into CI, and do not delete them either: only 2 of 109 lack an expect(), so as a SCRIPT for
    the manual pass they are worth more than re-deriving those cases by hand each UAT.
  </status-note>
</task>
